hip-load-oom: a fix to intel/llvm v7.2.0, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

A module the GPU has no room for is refused by hipModuleLoadDataEx as hipErrorNoBinaryForGpu (ROCm 10.1 on
an RX 9060 XT, with every block of its memory taken), which the HIP adapter passed on as a build failure.
The SYCL runtime keeps a failed build in its program cache and throws it again for every later use of the
program, so the kernels of a program first used while the GPU was full never ran in that process, also
after the memory was free again (an image engine started beside a text model whose expert cache held the
VRAM: every image job failed, "The program was built for 1 devices").  Out of device memory is not kept:
the runtime drops its cache and builds the program again at the next use.  Fixed, a load refused as having
no binary or no memory while the device has less than 256 MiB and twice the binary free is reported as out
of device memory.
---
--- a/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/program.cpp
+++ b/unified-runtime/source/adapters/hip/program.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 // Exceptions. See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
 // Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: HIP exit cleanup.
+// Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: HIP load OOM.
 //
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
@@ -249,8 +250,29 @@
   Options[3] = hipJitOptionErrorLogBufferSizeBytes;
   OptionVals[3] = (void *)(long)MAX_LOG_SIZE;
 
-  UR_CHECK_ERROR(hipModuleLoadDataEx(&Module, static_cast<const void *>(Binary),
-                                     NumberOfOptions, Options, OptionVals));
+  const hipError_t Loaded =
+      hipModuleLoadDataEx(&Module, static_cast<const void *>(Binary),
+                          NumberOfOptions, Options, OptionVals);
+  // A module the device has no room for (its code and data are placed in
+  // VRAM) is refused as hipErrorNoBinaryForGpu, which reads as a build
+  // failure: the SYCL runtime caches that for the program, and its kernels
+  // never ran in the process, even once the memory was free again.  Out of
+  // device memory, which the SYCL runtime does not cache, when the device is
+  // that full (ROCm 10.1, RX 9060 XT: a module with 64 MiB of data while every
+  // block was taken; an image engine started beside a text model holding the
+  // VRAM)
+  if (Loaded == hipErrorNoBinaryForGpu || Loaded == hipErrorOutOfMemory) {
+    size_t Free = 0, Total = 0;
+    if (hipMemGetInfo(&Free, &Total) == hipSuccess &&
+        Free < (size_t(256) << 20) + 2 * BinarySizeInBytes) {
+      UR_LOG(ERR,
+             "HIP module load: {} with {} MiB of device memory free: "
+             "out of device memory",
+             hipGetErrorName(Loaded), Free >> 20);
+      throw UR_RESULT_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY;
+    }
+  }
+  UR_CHECK_ERROR(Loaded);
   watchProcessExit();
 
   BuildStatus = UR_PROGRAM_BUILD_STATUS_SUCCESS;
